  "details": "VRChat SDK Version: 2021.01.28.19.08\nVRChat Client Version: Latest\nDescription of the bug:\nWhen I upload a private Avatar targeted to Android using the same pipeline as the PC version (so that the same Avatar can appear on both PC & Quest), it causes a weird glitch where my name tag and profile in the instance to appear as a \"Quest User\" to other people for a short time.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1. Exit VRChat while wearing an Avatar that you plan to update with a Quest-compatible version in Unity.\n2. Copy the Blueprint ID from the PC Unity project to the Android Unity project as required containing the Quest-optimized Avatar.\n3. Update your Quest Avatar to the same pipeline as the PC version, as usual.\n4. Log in to VRChat.\n5. Game loads the updated Avatar as previously equipped.\n6. Ask a friend if they see you labeled \"Quest\" user on either the Name Tag or in the Instance via Social Menu.\n7. If yes, restart VRChat and you'll be reverted back to appearing as a \"PC User.\"\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\nI have an output log related to the event that I can provide for further details, which was right after I updated my avatar and then joined a public instance where I talked to my friend who noticed the glitch.",
